ciaries are the communities in the State and tourists that would benet from the construction of bridges, slope protection, retrotting of hospital buildings, strengthening of SDRF &amp; re services, management of forest res, strengthening early warning system &amp; response capacity. It also includes research studies to plan the public expenditure with respect to climate considerations and also proposes for Road Asset Management &amp; sustainable management for forest biomass for generating livelihood through community participation. By strengthening disaster risk management systems and institutions the Project has the potential to benet the entire State of Uttarakhand.</p>', '<header id=\"header\" class=\"\">\r\n<section class=\"container-fluid d-flex align-items-center justify-content-between top-bar py-2\"><nav class=\"navbar\">\r\n<div class=\"container-xxl\">\r\n<p>Uttarakhand Disaster Recovery Project (UDRP) and Additional Financing (AF) have been implemented by the Government of Uttarakhand since 2013, with funding from the World Bank. This project focused on various aspects such as the restoration of housing and rural connectivity, riverbanks protection works, enhancing community resilience, and strengthening the state\'s emergency response capabilities.</p>\r\n<p>Uttarakhand Disaster Preparedness and Resilience Project (U-PREPARE) constitutes a large multi-sectoral engagement on risk and vulnerability reduction with assistance for reconstructing damaged resilient infrastructure, restoring connectivity, enhancing medical health facilities, strengthening SDRF &amp; Fire services, early warning &amp; response system, establishing Hydro meteorological network, strengthening &amp; upgradation of State command and Control Centre of Forest department, upgradation of existing &amp; construction of new Forest Crew Stations and improving technical support for managing future disaster risks. The Project design has incorporated lessons learned from previous national and global post-disaster recovery projects to ensure that the recovery is targeted, eective and is built back &ldquo;smarter&rdquo; in order to build resilience of local communities to future disasters.</p>\r\n<p>The primary beneciaries are the communities in the State and tourists that would benet from the construction of bridges, slope protection, retrotting of hospital buildings, strengthening of SDRF &amp; re services, management of forest res, strengthening early warning system &amp; response capacity. It also includes research studies to plan the public expenditure with respect to climate considerations and also proposes for Road Asset Management &amp; sustainable management for forest biomass for generating livelihood through community participation. By strengthening disaster risk management systems and institutions the Project has the potential to benet the entire State of Uttarakhand.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</nav></section>\r\n</header>', 'About U-PREPARE', NULL, NULL, 1, '2025-08-17 23:04:38', '2025-09-20 02:23:31', NULL),
(2, 'Mission and Vision', NULL, 'mission-and-vision', '', '', 'Mission and Vision', '', '', 0, '2025-08-17 23:04:52', '2025-11-18 05:20:21', NULL),
(3, 'History', 'History', 'history', '<p>The GoUK has implemented the World Bank assisted Uttarakhand Disaster Recovery Project (UDRP) and Additional Financing (AF) since 2013. UDRP-AF, which closed in September 2023.</p>\r\n<p>The project covered the restoration of housing and rural connectivity (roads, bridges &amp; slope protection work), River bank protection works, built the resilience of communities, and increased the capacity of the State to respond to emergencies.</p>\r\n<p>The Uttarakhand Disaster Preparedness and Resilience Project (U-PREPARE) is a large multi-sectoral engagement on risk and vulnerability reduction, with assistance for reconstructing damaged resilient infrastructure, restoring connectivity, enhancing medical health facilities, strengthening SDRF and Fire services, early warning and response system, establishing hydro meteorological network, strengthening and upgrading the State Command and Control Centre of Forest Department.</p>', '<p>The GoUK has implemented the World Bank assisted Uttarakhand Disaster Recovery Project (UDRP) and Additional Financing (AF) since 2013. UDRP-AF, which closed in September 2023.</p>\r\n<p>The project covered the restoration of housing and rural connectivity (roads, bridges &amp; slope protection work), River bank protection works, built the resilience of communities, and increased the capacity of the State to respond to emergencies.</p>\r\n<p>The Uttarakhand Disaster Preparedness and Resilience Project (U-PREPARE) is a large multi-sectoral engagement on risk and vulnerability reduction, with assistance for reconstructing damaged resilient infrastructure, restoring connectivity, enhancing medical health facilities, strengthening SDRF and Fire services, early warning and response system, establishing hydro meteorological network, strengthening and upgrading the State Command and Control Centre of Forest Department.</p>', 'History', NULL, NULL, 1, '2025-08-17 23:05:05', '2025-11-18 05:01:36', NULL),
(4, 'Objectives', NULL, 'objectives', '<ul>\r\n<li>to prioritize climate and disaster-resilient infrastructure and include resilience into infrastructure development.</li>\r\n<li>to strengthen the ability of Uttarakhand\'s government institutions and first responders to forecast, plan for, and respond to catastrophes.</li>\r\n<li>to improve the Uttarakhand government and local communities\' ability to prevent and control forest and general fires.</li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul>\r\n<li>to prioritize climate and disaster-resilient infrastructure and include resilience into infrastructure development.</li>\r\n<li>to strengthen the ability of Uttarakhand\'s government institutions and first responders to forecast, plan for, and respond to catastrophes.</li>\r\n<li>to improve the Uttarakhand government and local communities\' ability to prevent and control forest and general fires.</li>\r\n</ul>', 'Objectives', NULL, NULL, 1, '2025-08-17 23:05:17', '2025-09-19 23:31:44', NULL),
(5, 'Project Structure', NULL, 'project-structure', '', '', 'Project Structure', '', '', 1, '2025-08-17 23:05:31', '2025-08-17 23:05:31', NULL),
(6, 'Enhancing Infrastructure Resilience', NULL, 'enhancing-infrastructure-resilience', '<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left: 7.1pt; mso-add-space: auto; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">a)<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">Enhancing the resilience of transport connectivity, through </strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>improving the condition, safety, and resilience of select bridges that are prone to floods;&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>reducing the risks of landslides to enhance population safety, including scaling up bioengineering solutions;</li>\r\n<li>supporting the new Uttarakhand Landslide Mitigation and Management Centre (ULMMC) achieve its vision of becoming a center of excellence for landslide risk management, including through capacity building, preparing an institutional development plan, and promoting the application of technology and innovation; and</li>\r\n<li>strengthening the capacity of the PWD in resilient design and construction, developing a PWD Climate Adaptation Policy, which will integrate disaster and climate risk management approaches into existing systems, and developing a Road Asset Management System with a climate module.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left: 7.1pt; mso-add-space: auto; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">b)<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">Providing disaster shelter, through&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>conducting a shelter needs and development assessment in the context of climate change;&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>constructing pilot multipurpose disaster shelters in selected disaster-prone areas along major routes with resilient, inclusive, and energy-efficient designs; and</li>\r\n<li>establishing institutions and procedures for shelter management including the use and maintenance of the shelters during non-emergency situations.</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left: 7.1pt; mso-add-space: auto; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">a)<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">Enhancing the resilience of transport connectivity, through </strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>improving the condition, safety, and resilience of select bridges that are prone to floods;&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>reducing the risks of landslides to enhance population safety, including scaling up bioengineering solutions;</li>\r\n<li>supporting the new Uttarakhand Landslide Mitigation and Management Centre (ULMMC) achieve its vision of becoming a center of excellence for landslide risk management, including through capacity building, preparing an institutional development plan, and promoting the application of technology and innovation; and</li>\r\n<li>strengthening the capacity of the PWD in resilient design and construction, developing a PWD Climate Adaptation Policy, which will integrate disaster and climate risk management approaches into existing systems, and developing a Road Asset Management System with a climate module.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"margin-left: 7.1pt; mso-add-space: auto; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-latin;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">b)<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\">Providing disaster shelter, through&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>conducting a shelter needs and development assessment in the context of climate change;&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>constructing pilot multipurpose disaster shelters in selected disaster-prone areas along major routes with resilient, inclusive, and energy-efficient designs; and</li>\r\n<li>establishing institutions and procedures for shelter management including the use and maintenance of the shelters during non-emergency situations.</li>\r\n</ul>', 'Enhancing Infrastructure Resilience', NULL, NULL, 1, '2025-08-17 23:06:01', '2025-09-20 02:38:39', NULL),
(7, 'Improving Emergency Preparedness and Response', NULL, 'improving-emergency-preparedness-and-response', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;\"><span style=\"mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri;\">This component will support improving the capabilities of Uttarakhand&rsquo;s government entities and first responders to predict, prepare for, and respond to disasters, through:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: \'Calibri-Bold\',sans-serif; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri-Bold;\">&nbsp;</span></strong><strong><span style=\"font-family: \'Calibri-Bold\',sans-serif; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri-Bold;\">(a) Strengthening emergency preparedness, </span></strong><span style=\"mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri;\">through </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;\"><span style=\"mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri;\">(i) establishing a State Emergency Operations Center with a Centralized Incident Command</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;\"><span style=\"mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri;\">System to enhance coordination; </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;\"><span style=\"mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri;\">(ii) reviewing and strengthening the Uttarakhand&rsquo;s multi-agency institutional emergency and response frameworks and SOPs; and </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;\"><span style=\"mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri;\">(iii) implementing community DRM activities.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: \'Calibri-Bold\',sans-serif; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri-Bold;\">&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: \'Calibri-Bold\',sans-serif; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri-Bold;\">(b) Strengthening hydromet and early warning systems (EWS) </span></strong><span style=\"mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri;\">through </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;\"><span style=\"mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri;\">(i) improving impact forecasting for weather, climate, and hydrological hazards; </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;\"><span style=\"mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri;\">(ii) establishing an end-to-end multi-hazard EWS to provide timely warnings directly to the vulnerable population, using multi-channel and multi-technology dissemination systems; </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;\"><span style=\"mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri;\">(iii) developing fit-for-purpose hydromet tools and services for stakeholders in key sectors; and (iv) training and capacity building for DRM officials at state and local levels and communities.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: \'Calibri-Bold\',sans-serif; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri-Bold;\">&nbsp;</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;\"><strong><span style=\"font-family: \'Calibri-Bold\',sans-serif; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri-Bold;\">(c) Strengthening the State Disaster Response Force </span></strong><span style=\"mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri;\">through </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;\"><span style=\"mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri;\">(i) constructing SDRF outdoor search and rescue training facilities and sub-team stations;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;\"><span style=\"mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri;\">(ii) providing search and rescue and communications equipment; and </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: .0001pt; line-height: normal; mso-layout-grid-align: none; text-autospace: none;\"><span style=\"mso-ascii-font-family: Calibri; mso-hansi-font-family: Calibri; mso-bidi-font-family: Calibri;\">(iii) providing training on equipment storage, maintenance, and repair.</s